    "name": "assign_task",
    "description": "Hand the user a task only they can do, shown in their Standup panel across all sessions. Their answer comes back to you as a new message; do not wait for it.\nSome things only the user can do: put a secret or key in place, act on their machine or their accounts, make a decision that is theirs, review or approve something. For each of those, call assign_task, even when you also asked about it in your reply; a question asked only in prose is easy to miss when they run many sessions. A secret or key you do not have is always a task: never ask for it in chat.\nBut when the user has already given a standing permission for that kind of action (memory, CLAUDE.md, settings, or a yes earlier in this conversation), do not ask: do it, and end your reply with one line saying what you did and which permission covered it.\nkind: \"do\" (they go do it and press Done), \"answer\" (they write a few words), \"choose\" (2-4 options). Title: one short imperative line. Detail: what exactly, where, and how you will know it is done. At most 5 open tasks per session; the same ask is never assigned twice."
   },
